Option
T}@T{
Meaning
T}
_
T{
\f[B]--force\f[R]
T}@T{
Overwrite files that were edited since
the last export, or never written by
\f[B]ari\f[R]
T}
.TE
.SH TUI
.PP
\f[B]ari\f[R] with no command, when
input and output are both a terminal,
opens a list of every host, or of the
inventory \f[B]-i\f[R] names.
It reads config.toml and the inventories
before the screen changes, so a missing
config, a broken inventory or an
undeclared \f[B]-i\f[R] is an error, as
for any command.
.PP
The list shows NAME, HOSTNAME, USER,
INV, a column per module as in
\f[B]ls\f[R], and GROUPS.
The filter above it narrows the list as
you type and matches what \f[B]ls
--search\f[R] matches.
The cursor stays on its host while the
filter changes, as long as the host
still matches.
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
lw(24.5n) lw(45.5n).
